{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "הצפוני", :translit "ha-tzfoni", :gloss "the northern one"} {:he "ואת הצפוני ארחיק מעליכם", :translit "v'et ha-tzfoni archik m'aleichem", :gloss "and the northern one I will distance from you"} {:he "שיתבטל יצר הרע", :translit "she-yitbatel yetzer ha-ra", :gloss "that the evil inclination will be nullified"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הצפוני" "ואת הצפוני ארחיק מעליכם"]}], :frame {:text "The phrase ואת הצפוני ארחיק מעליכם appears in Ezekiel 48:1, where הצפוני is part of the tribal allotment description. Elijah is identified as from the tribe of Gad in the genealogy of 1 Kings 17:1. The link between Elijah and the tribe of Gad is drawn by Ba'al HaTurim from the occurrence of הצפוני both here in the Gadite census and in Ezekiel's prophecy. The tradition that the evil inclination will be nullified in the future is found in Sukkah 52a.", :sources ["Ezekiel 48:1" "1 Kings 17:1" "Sukkah 52a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "לצפון", :translit "l'tzafon", :gloss "to the north"} {:he "צפיון", :translit "tzifyon", :gloss "Tzifyon (a Gadite clan name)"} {:he "צפון", :translit "tzafun", :gloss "hidden / north"} {:he "צפון בחלקו", :translit "tzafun b'chelko", :gloss "hidden in his portion"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Wordplay: לצפון / צפיון / צפון share the root צ-פ-ן"}], :frame {:text "The verse reads לצפון (Numbers 26:15), the name of a Gadite clan, while the parallel passage in Genesis 46:16 lists the same clan as צפיון. Moses received the Ten Commandments at Sinai (Exodus 20:2–14). Moses's burial place remains unknown, described in Deuteronomy 34:6 as a valley in the land of Moab opposite Beth-peor, where no one knows his grave to this day.", :sources ["Numbers 26:15" "Genesis 46:16" "Deuteronomy 34:6"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["הצפוני" "ואת הצפוני ארחיק מעליכם"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "הצפוני", :refs ["Numbers 26:15" "Joel 2:20"], :n 2, :lens :exact} {:ph